# BFO relations as used by PMD: a precedes b, b precedes c, c precedes a. 'x precedes y' = the end of x is not after the start of y (before or meets).
# No pair of these facts is contradictory; the cycle is (composition).
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix ex: <http://ex.org/> .

ex:a obo:BFO_0000063 ex:b .
ex:b obo:BFO_0000063 ex:c .
ex:c obo:BFO_0000063 ex:a .
